### Open follow-ups

- aide_brain remediation text for no-mcp-entry/mcp-drift (and the aide_info description) tells the user to run `npx … sync` themselves. This conflicts with the brain.md anti-pattern. It is pre-existing and not fixed in this cycle.
- The installAgents spec claims the kanban skill outcome, but installSkills stages it (scope attribution).
- brain.md Step 3's malformed branch wording fits syntax faults better than read errors.
- The user's global ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md and the design-handoff / handoff:start skills still reference the old kb:* skills. They need updating to /kanban, which requires the user's OK for their private config.
- brain.md's malformed branch should say an unknown marker may be a retired section to delete. Example: work-kanban from the unpublished d41c3c5 template.
- The narrowed banned-vocabulary invariant's wording is loose. Phrase it as "backend-specific tool names and link syntax outside the template".
- The user's brain has a stray `kanban/doing/` folder (1 card), and board/folder drift (In Progress 17 lines vs 19 files; Done 10 vs 100+). /kanban manage reconciles it.
- The behind check ignores `npm_config_registry`.
- Upgrade and sync wording for malformed or unreadable brain.aide.
- Specs are missing for the helper orchestrators (resolveBehind, resolveLaunchModes, obsidianBrainAideTemplate, extractMarkerSections).
- wireMcp runs the package check even when the entry exists.
- Flaky ~5s install-suite tests.
- Session-cwd root-resolution bug (separate card candidate).
- The README Quick Start still describes the retired `--vault-path`.
- The user's `design-handoff` skill mentions `npx @aidemd-mcp/server@latest sync`.
- This repo's own .aide/config/brain.aide predates the 15-section contract and will report brain-aide-invalid (missing sections) on the next /aide boot here — expected; repair via /aide:brain config.

## Process discipline (permanent)

- One implementor per numbered plan step.
- .claude/ files are edited directly, never pipelined.
- Pause for user approval before the build.

